1
00:00:06,419 --> 00:00:11,740
Type 2 Diabetes is a condition in which your blood sugar level is too high.

2
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:16,480
Carbohydrates are substances your body uses to make energy.

3
00:00:17,039 --> 00:00:22,379
After you eat food that contains carbohydrates, it eventually goes to your small intestine.

4
00:00:23,260 --> 00:00:29,280
In your small intestine, the food is broken down into single sugar molecules called glucose.

5
00:00:30,359 --> 00:00:35,960
The cells in your small intestine soak up the sugars, which pass into your bloodstream.

6
00:00:36,619 --> 00:00:41,539
When the blood reaches your pancreas, it detects the high amount of sugar in your blood.

7
00:00:42,039 --> 00:00:47,579
Normally, this causes your pancreas to put a chemical called insulin into your bloodstream.

8
00:00:48,219 --> 00:00:52,659
The insulin reduces the amount of sugar in your blood to a healthy level.

9
00:00:53,979 --> 00:00:55,439
How does insulin do this?

10
00:00:56,799 --> 00:01:02,960
As the blood moves through your body, the insulin and sugar exit the bloodstream into your tissues

11
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:09,879
to reach your cells. Most cells have structures on their surfaces called insulin receptors.

12
00:01:10,560 --> 00:01:13,920
When insulin flows by, it attaches to the receptors.

13
00:01:14,879 --> 00:01:18,739
The insulin acts like a key in a lock to open up the cell.

14
00:01:21,280 --> 00:01:23,480
So the sugar can get inside.

15
00:01:24,640 --> 00:01:29,200
Now your cell can use the sugar to make the energy it needs to work properly.

16
00:01:30,060 --> 00:01:33,459
And your blood sugar level drops back to its normal range.

17
00:01:35,519 --> 00:01:40,939
If you have type 2 diabetes, your cells don't respond to insulin as they should.

18
00:01:40,939 --> 00:01:43,299
This is called insulin resistance.

19
00:01:44,439 --> 00:01:49,859
When this happens, your insulin cannot unlock the cells to let sugar in,

20
00:01:49,959 --> 00:01:54,500
because the locks or insulin receptors are missing or aren't working.

21
00:01:57,640 --> 00:02:01,700
As a result, sugar is locked out of your cells.

22
00:02:05,659 --> 00:02:10,319
When sugar can't get into your cells, it builds up in your bloodstream.

23
00:02:10,939 --> 00:02:14,039
This is a condition called hyperglycemia.

24
00:02:16,219 --> 00:02:21,740
In response to the high blood sugar levels, your pancreas makes more and more insulin.

25
00:02:22,419 --> 00:02:25,659
The overworked cells in your pancreas try to keep up.

26
00:02:27,099 --> 00:02:30,340
But they slowly lose their ability to make enough insulin.

27
00:02:30,939 --> 00:02:34,560
These problems may lead to the symptoms of type 2 diabetes.

28
00:02:36,979 --> 00:02:42,740
If you have questions about type 2 diabetes or any medications you have been prescribed,

29
00:02:43,080 --> 00:02:44,139
speak with your doctor.

30
00:02:44,580 --> 00:02:48,400
It is important to take your medications as directed by your doctor,

31
00:02:48,840 --> 00:02:52,120
tell him or her about any side effects you have.

